Hello Carine,

Can you please send the exact offending call that is triggering the error together with the output of calling summary() on your data object?

In general, population size (as opposed to the pseudo-population size) should correspond to the size of the population network (which is not observed in its entirety) you want to make inferences about and from which you sampled the egos. This inference is the main goal of the model implemented in ergm.ego. If such a population network does not exist or is hard to conceive as a theoretical device it might be difficult to interpret (some of) the results. What's the purpose of your analysis?

Best,
Micha?


